Z||000000||Makaio13||03-12-2001||07:26 PM||||I just aquired an 85 Fiero GT and I am intersted in converting it to a Fiero MERA.  Is this possible?  I know people have converted their Fiero's to Ferrari 328 GTSs but is there a kit available to do so?  I was hoping someone a little more experienced in this field could shed some light on this.  Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||rogergarrison||03-12-2001||07:34 PM||||the Mera is a built kit by Pontiac, there is no kit. Most Ferrari kits are no longer available. Unbuilt kits are getting really rare. One that seems to be most prevalent is the 355. Check in ebay, i just saw several 355 kits and a testa rossa go for less than $3000. I just made a post about a BB512 finished kit for sale in Okla. They are EXTREMELY rare. I build my 308 over last 3 years. so feel free to email me about anything.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=9116379&p=34556781"> ||||reg||1
