Z||000005||pherder||03-12-2001||09:23 PM||||This IS NOT MINE but I was the first owner of one of Custom Coachcraft's 308 kits (mine was used as the demo car and made it into May 96 issue of Kit Car Magazine!)<P><B>Ad No.: 104 - Subject: 308 Ferrari Kit for Sale - Posted on: 01/17/01<BR>Reply to: Bill Clark at wclark@nj.com<BR>Custom Coachcraft 308 Ferrari kit with: Rodney Dickman front bumper, real<BR>Ferrari lights and badges, 1987 Fiero SE (V-6, 5-speed, all power - many new<BR>parts) and complete Auto Design interior kit. Complete details and pictures<BR>available. A GREAT deal at $6,750.</B><P>The cost of <B>JUST</B> the parts would be way over the $6750 he is asking for!  I spent $4000 on the Auto Designs interior, $400+ on Rodney's bumper, and the real Ferrari lights and badges is somewhere around $700!!!  Not to mention the kit price in 1996 was $4500 and you would get a loaded 87 GT 5 speed with it!!!<P>Good luck!<P>Paul<BR>------------------<BR>88 Formula<BR>88 Coupe<BR>86 SE<BR>95 GMC<BR>92 Mazda<BR>55 Jones<BR>Sedgwick, KS 67135<BR>pherder@kscable.com<p>[This message has been edited by pherder (edited 03-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||rockcrawl||03-12-2001||09:31 PM||||Ferrari has always been really tough on replica manufacturers. There are still a lot of them around, but they have been forced into the kitcar underground. They cannot advertise for fear of being sued. I've seen very many kits of all kinds on Ebay lately, it seems like a safe way for them to get publicity.... for now. But anyway, you can't build a Mera, but you can build a 308 replica. Honestly I don't know how GM ever sold the Mera without a lawsuit.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ferrarisues_2.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||03-12-2001||10:20 PM||||Rodneys the resident expert on Mera I think. I seem to remember him saying they only made 2 years, i think it was something like 280? total. I know for a while the same company that made the wheels for Mera made the real ones for Ferrari, and Ferrari threatened to stop using them because of it.||||reg||1
